# New Admin Account Detection

## Objective

Identify accounts that have been assigned privileged administrative roles in Microsoft Entra ID.

## MITRE ATT&CK

- T1098 - Account Manipulation

## KQL Query

```kusto
AuditLogs
| where OperationName contains "Add member to role"
| extend InitiatedByUser = tostring(InitiatedBy.user.userPrincipalName)
| extend TargetUser = tostring(TargetResources[0].userPrincipalName)
| extend RoleAssigned = tostring(TargetResources[0].displayName)
| project
    TimeGenerated,
    InitiatedByUser,
    TargetUser,
    RoleAssigned,
    Result
| order by TimeGenerated desc
```

## Data Source

- AuditLogs
- Microsoft Entra ID

## Threat Scenario

An attacker obtains administrative privileges by assigning privileged roles to a compromised account.

## Analyst Investigation Steps

1. Identify who assigned the role.
2. Verify whether the assignment was approved.
3. Review recent activities of the target user.
4. Check authentication logs for suspicious activity.
5. Remove unauthorized privileges if necessary.

## Expected Findings

- Unauthorized role assignment
- Privilege escalation attempt
- Insider threat activity
- Compromised administrative account

## Severity

High

## MITRE Mapping

| Tactic | Technique |
|---------|---------|
| Persistence | T1098 |
| Privilege Escalation | T1098 |

## Remediation

- Remove unauthorized administrative access.
- Reset affected credentials.
- Review privileged role assignments.
- Enable MFA for privileged accounts.
- Monitor future role modifications.
```
